WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
May 1968. A general strike
by millions of workers.

2
00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:07.840
Out of it come the «accords de Grenelle»:

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:10.510
the minimum wage goes up by 35 per cent.

4
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:15.860
2023: 14 national days of
strikes and marches against

5
00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:18.460
raising the pension age to 64.

6
00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:23.170
And a word trap: «une
manifestation» is a protest march.

7
00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.680
So why the 35-hour week,

8
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.230
and what really happens when
French workers go on strike?

9
00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:32.610
In this mission, you'll walk
a timeline of French strikes.

10
00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.280
Then you'll compare
what women and men earn,

11
00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:37.180
one bar at a time.

12
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:41.170
Your mission: find out why
France has a 35-hour week,

13
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:43.150
and what a strike really means there.
